All right, I'm back from playing a wizard mode game, to present to you these
wonderous bugs I have found.

Machine:  Macintosh IIcx, color, 5 meg ram, running system 6.0.3 and
multifinder.

Nice to see that there are no (obvious) mulitfinder bugs.

Noninteresting bugs:  The version command says patchlevel 6 (but gives a 
   likely-looking compiled date)

   If you move onto a friendly monster and it asks you whether you want to
     attack or not, and you say no, and you are invisible, it creates a
     perminant inverse spot where you were that lasts until the next screen
     update.  Come to think of it, I don't know whether this happens when you
     aren't invisible or not.  Teach me to use wizard mode...

   When you eat a mimic corpse in a shop, it costs you 1 gold piece.  When you
     pay for it, you pay for "a partially-eaten {small/large} mimic corpse.

Interesting/nasty bugs:

   Climbing stairs (not in wizard mode) from 5 to 4.  A robbed shop and cops
     on level 4.  It crashed.  Badly.  Macsbug said something very close to:

     Unimplimented instruction at 0073C368
     (inquiry by yours truly revealed)
     Address 0073C368 is in RAM, but not in system or Application heaps.
     The heap at 0038A16C is bad 
        Block length is bad
     Block header

     Unable to access that address.

     I am not sure whether the 0038... has anything to do with it, since I don't
       really know how Macsbug or C works.  And I haven't been able to
       reproduce the bug, for lack of a shop on level 4.  Other levels haven't
       done this to me.  Fluke?

   Climbing downstairs from the medusa level (24, I think), nethack just up
     and quit (out of memory error).  It was set in multifinder for 750K.  I
     assume it wants more, and gave it 1 meg.  Or is this an actual bug, and
     it shouldn't need any more memory?  Anyway, wasn't able to repeat it,
     because this wan't wizard mode and I was busy tearing hair out, etc.  
     And I didn't back up my save file.  AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHHHHHHH!!

   Congrads guys.  Anything this large that has this few bugs is amazing.

